<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Filet launcher icon — foreground layer.  Candidate E4, chosen 2026-09-13.

  Two-tone open folder.  Body in the shade colour, flap in the accent.

  The gap between the two shapes is INHERENT, not masked: the body path stops at
  y=46 and the flap starts at y=53.  That is deliberate — VectorDrawable has no
  mask support, and more importantly the monochrome layer collapses both shapes to
  one colour, so a gap faked with a background-coloured shape on top would fill in
  and the mark would become a blob.  Never reintroduce one.

  Canvas 108x108, safe zone x/y 18..90.

  The paths are drawn at their natural size, which spans x 16..92 - four units
  WIDER than the safe zone - and a group scales them to fit rather than the
  coordinates being rewritten.  Two reasons for the group: the numbers stay
  readable as the shape someone drew, and the scale is one value to change if the
  mark is ever redrawn.

  This was measured, not assumed.  The comment here used to assert every edge was
  already inside the safe zone; it was not, the body reached x=16 and the flap
  x=92, and an aggressively-masking launcher clipped both.  tools/check-icon.mjs
  now flattens the paths, computes the bounds and fails if they leave the zone, so
  the claim cannot drift back into being decorative.

  THE SQUARE IS NOT THE BINDING CONSTRAINT.  Circle, squircle and teardrop masks
  are all inscribed in the 72x72 viewport, and what they share is the 66dp CIRCLE -
  radius 33 about the centre.  A mark that fills the square loses its left and
  right extremes to a round launcher, which is exactly what the splash screen was
  showing: the folder rendered as a bowl.

  Three scales were rendered under both masks and looked at, not reasoned about:

    0.945  fills the square.  On a circle the folder loses both side edges and
           stops reading as a folder at all.
    0.800  SHIPPED.  On a circle only the outer corners of the flap are kissed;
           it still reads unmistakably as a folder, and on a squircle it is as
           bold as before.
    0.697  measured as the largest scale whose INK never leaves the circle.
           Safe, and visibly timid - a small mark adrift in dead margin.

  0.8 is a judgement, and it is one number to change if Nic wants it bolder or
  safer.  check-icon.mjs still prints how far the mark reaches on every run, so
  whichever way it moves, the cost is on screen rather than in someone's head.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <!-- 0.8 about the canvas centre. Not the 0.945 that merely fits the square:
         see the header - a round mask is the binding constraint, not the square one. -->
    <group
        android:pivotX="54"
        android:pivotY="54"
        android:scaleX="0.8"
        android:scaleY="0.8">

        <!-- body + tab (shade) -->
        <path
            android:fillColor="#4E7382"
            android:pathData="M26,24h16l6,8h30a6,6 0 0 1 6,6v8H16V30a6,6 0 0 1 6,-6z" />

        <!-- front flap (accent) -->
        <path
            android:fillColor="#7FA8B8"
            android:pathData="M24,53h64a4,4 0 0 1 3.9,4.9l-5.6,24A6,6 0 0 1 80.4,86H21a4,4 0 0 1 -3.9,-4.9l5.6,-24A6,6 0 0 1 24,53z" />
    </group>

</vector>
